# CapExIQ Environment Variables Template
#
# GRACEFUL DEGRADATION (important)
# --------------------------------
# Every route under /api/ai/ works with NO environment configuration at all.
# When OPENAI_API_KEY is absent — or the model call times out, errors, or
# returns output that fails schema validation — each route returns HTTP 200
# with a deterministic advisory response generated from the pre-computed
# figures of the finance engine. It never returns a 500 for a missing key.
#
# Every AI response carries three provenance fields so the UI can label it:
#   isFallback     : boolean
#   source         : "model" | "deterministic"
#   fallbackReason : "none" | "no-api-key" | "model-error" | "invalid-model-output"
#
# The application is therefore fully demonstrable without any API key. The
# deterministic path is the default, not an error path.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# API key for the AI advisory routes. Server-side route handlers only.
# IMPORTANT: never use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix for secrets — that would ship
# the key to the browser bundle.
# Leave unset to run the whole application on the deterministic engine.
OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-proj-your-openai-api-key-here"

# Chat model used by every AI advisory route handler.
# Optional — the routes fall back to "gpt-4o" when this is unset.
OPENAI_MODEL="gpt-4o"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI route inventory (all under /api/ai/, all POST, all Zod-validated)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# explain          natural-language Q&A over the model
# recommend        structured board recommendation JSON
# threat-radar     ranked archetype-specific risk axes with mitigations
# board-debate     simulated capital committee (CFO / COO / CRO / NED) + synthesis
# board-memo       full board memorandum draft in structured sections
# scenario-studio  proposes extra named scenarios as multiplier sets (engine evaluates)
# esg-impact       ESG / green-financing commentary; flags notApplicable for
#                  ai-platform, new-product and online-service archetypes
# parse-quote      extracts capex line items from pasted vendor quotations
# live-macro       reasons over macro data SUPPLIED IN THE REQUEST; no live market access
# voice-intent     maps a transcript to a structured app intent, or "unknown"
#
# Shared guardrails live in src/lib/ai/guardrails.ts:
#   - 2,000-character cap on every free-text field
#   - prompt-injection delimiting of all user-supplied text
#   - max_tokens cap (800; 1,600 for the two long-form memo/debate routes)
#   - AbortSignal.timeout(30000) on every model call
#   - generic client-facing error messages; detail logged server-side only
#   - the AI layer never computes a financial figure
